It was my own fault, of course; I honestly forgot I'd already come up
a level. Still, I partly blame the RNG: when was the last time any of
you made it that far without seeing even one lonely blindfold? The
lack of levitation I can understand at least, but gods, in most games
I have to bloody well *kick* towels out of my way in general stores.

Ah well. It was my best game yet, and maybe someday I'll actually get
as far as Gehennom. I can't say I'm exactly looking forward to it. (I
played a wizard-mode game as far as the VotD once; I shudder to think
of facing it without my ^W'd AC of -92. Heh.)

As a closing aside, I hear from everyone that Valks are the easiest
character class--my own experiences certainly bear this out--but I
haven't been able to figure out why. What do they have that other
classes don't?

